.TH PRUDENCE 1 "2026-04-13" "prudence 0.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
prudence \- move files to the XDG trash and restore them later
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B prudence
[\-\-]
.IR path ...
.br
.B prudence
.B list
.br
.B prudence
.B clear
.br
.B prudence
.B restore
.IR entry-id | entry-name ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B prudence
moves files and directories into the freedesktop.org trash layout instead of deleting
them permanently.
It can also list existing trash entries and restore them to their recorded original paths.
It can permanently clear the trash contents on demand.
.PP
For files on the same filesystem as the home data directory,
.B prudence
uses
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/Trash
or
.IR $HOME/.local/share/Trash .
For other mounted filesystems, it uses
.IR $topdir/.Trash/$uid
or
.IR $topdir/.Trash\-$uid .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "prudence " path ...
Move one or more files or directories into the trash.
Use
.B \-\-
before a path that begins with
.BR - .
.TP
.B prudence list
Print the current trash entries in a readable multi-line format with a stable ID,
trashed name, deletion time, and recorded original path.
.TP
.B prudence clear
Permanently remove the current trash contents.
.TP
.BI "prudence restore " entry-id | entry-name ...
Restore one or more entries from the trash.
Entries may be selected by the stable ID from
.B prudence list
or by exact trashed name.
If a name is ambiguous, an ID must be used instead.
.SH SAFETY
.TP
.B No permanent delete during trashing
Moving files into the trash does not permanently delete them.
.TP
.B Explicit clear
Permanent deletion only happens when
.B prudence clear
is used.
.TP
.B Root protection
It refuses to trash a filesystem root.
.TP
.B No overwrite on restore
It refuses to restore over an existing path.
.TP
.B Cross-filesystem fallback
If a direct rename is not possible, it copies into the trash first and removes the
original only after the copy succeeds.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
prudence notes.txt old-dir
prudence -- -starts-with-dash
prudence list
prudence clear
prudence restore notes.txt
prudence restore home:notes.txt
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/Trash
Home trash location when
.I XDG_DATA_HOME
is set.
.TP
.I $HOME/.local/share/Trash
Fallback home trash location.
.TP
.I $topdir/.Trash/$uid
Mount-local trash when an administrator-created sticky
.I .Trash
directory exists.
.TP
.I $topdir/.Trash\-$uid
Mount-local fallback trash directory.
.SH INSTALLATION
To make
.B man prudence
work system-wide, install the manual page into a standard manpath, for example:
.PP
.nf
sudo install -d /usr/local/share/man/man1
sudo install -m 644 man/man1/prudence.1 /usr/local/share/man/man1/prudence.1
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR man (1)
